  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "15753492",
      "title": "Bug: run records store touched files as full paths, not paths relative to the project root",
      "status": "backlog",
      "componentId": "agent-tooling",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-08T20:33:57.586Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-08T20:34:08.103Z",
      "order": 16,
      "kind": "bug",
      "role": "backend-engineer",
      "description": "Proposed track: Bugfix. Plan: after decision-alerts (sprint 2026-w43). Not ready to build: needs the PM's track confirmation, then `specs/bugs/15753492/bugfix.md` and a failing regression test from the qa-engineer.\n\nObserved (EM, 2026-10-09): every `run.progress` event in `.project-log/*.jsonl` stores `touched` as a full path, for example `/Users/…/project-companion/specs/decision-alerts/design.md`.\nEffect: `lib/project/git-link.ts:152` compares `run.touched` with the commit's paths, which are relative to the root. So a run never links to its commits.\nWhere: the `ingest` path in `cli/index.ts` (~line 1184) passes the harness `touched` list to `reportRun` in `lib/project/store.ts` (~line 1489) unchanged.\nExpected: each touched path is stored relative to the project root. The requirement ID is for the qa-engineer to find; if none exists, write UNKNOWN and tell the EM.\nOpen for the spec: what to do with the full paths already in the log (read-time normalising, or leave them)."
    },
