    {
      "id": "8e6e5a71",
      "title": "Pass decision text to osascript only as arguments",
      "description": "da-t4. Criteria: DA-02.4 (argument half). Tests: 'DA-02.4: osascript passes every argument after -- unchanged' (required, darwin only); 'DA-02.4: notifierArgs gives 10 items, text only after --'; 'TH-3: notifierPath defaults to /usr/bin/osascript and takes the override' (both cases from design.md:445-446: the default, and PROJECT_COMPANION_NOTIFIER \"/x\" gives \"/x\"). Verify: npm test -- notify. Creates lib/project/notify.ts (constants, notifierPath, notifierArgs, dispatch). Lines: ~90 (source: architect hand-off; not checked). Depends on: da-t2.\n\nTest rule from the PR #10 security review (finding 1, TH-19, low; EM, 2026-10-09): the off switch guards only notifyDecision, not dispatch(program, args) (design.md:287). Tests call dispatch only with notifierPath(stubEnv(...)), never with NOTIFIER or notifierPath(process.env), or a test run can show a real banner on the PM's Mac. QA check at review: grep 'dispatch(' tests/notify.test.ts and confirm every call uses a stubEnv path. CI also runs on macos-latest (card c-18a31a), so there the off switch, not the platform check, stops dispatch.\n\nTest rule from the PR #11 reviews (security F2, low; EM, 2026-10-09; applies to da-t4 to da-t9): every env in tests/notify.test.ts spreads process.env or stubEnv(...), and no test overrides or removes PROJECT_COMPANION_NOTIFIER or PROJECT_COMPANION_NOTIFY after stubEnv (an empty notifier falls back to /usr/bin/osascript). Since PR #11, stubEnv accepts only a path inside the suite's temporary folder, and the suite stops at once when the off switch is not set. QA check at review: grep -nE 'PROJECT_COMPANION_NOTIF|env: *\\{|stubEnv\\(' tests/notify.test.ts. A grep for writes to process.env must end its pattern in =[^=], so that === does not match.\n\nRule changes from the PR #14 reviews (EM, 2026-10-09; apply to da-t4 to da-t9): (1) The env rule above applies to every env given to dispatch, notifyDecision or a child process; a plain object such as {} passed to the pure notifierPath is fine. (2) Since PR #14, dispatch refuses a program path that is not absolute (DispatchError step \"path\"). The one allowed dispatch call without a stubEnv path is a name that is not on PATH (for example pc-no-such-notifier), to test that refusal; it needs a one-line comment. (3) The suite also stops at once when STUB_OUT or STUB_HOLD is set in the environment.",
      "status": "done",
      "componentId": "notifier",
