    {
      "id": "6042a875",
      "title": "Prove a failed or slow notifier leaves the CLI unchanged",
      "description": "da-t8. Criteria: DA-02.1, DA-02.3; finishes DA-02.4 (stub half), DA-03.3 (CLI half) and the CLI half of TH-5. Tests: 'DA-02.1: same exit code and stdout as off'; 'DA-02.3: the CLI exits while the notifier waits'; 'DA-02.4: a hostile card question reaches the stub unchanged'; 'DA-03.3: linux and win32 give the same output as off'; 'TH-5: a folder in place of an approved artifact gives one stderr line and output as with off' (design 3.4, design.md:450-454); TH-21 CLI test. Verify: npm test -- notify. Lines: ~100 tests (source: architect hand-off ~90, plus ~10 for the TH-5 CLI test; not checked). Depends on: da-t7.\n\nTest rules from the PR #11 code review (notes, not findings; EM, 2026-10-09; also apply to da-t7): (1) Wait for <pid>.done before a test ends, and delete stub files with { force: true }. The STUB_OUT folder is shared, so a detached stub's late files can otherwise make the next test flaky. (2) DA-02.3: when the CLI exits, check that <pid>.argv exists and <pid>.done does not, then release the hold. Nothing in PR #11 tests the stub's wait. (3) The \"off\" comparison runs for DA-02.1 and DA-03.3 set PROJECT_COMPANION_NOTIFY: \"off\" in their own env (use stubEnv(STUB, { notify: \"off\" }) since PR #15). (4) The stub's hold loop stops after 600 polls (about 30 s at 0.05 s each); keep the test's guard timeout below that.\n\nNotes from the PR #16 code review (EM, 2026-10-09): (5) In the DA-02.1 run with a missing notifier, also check that stderr is exactly one line `project-companion: notification not sent: ENOENT <tmp>/missing`; that closes the CLI half of DA-02.2 for the cause the requirement names. If that run also breaks .project-notify, expect 2 lines, \"not sent\" first.",
      "status": "done",
      "componentId": "notifier",
      "featureId": "notify-safety",
      "phaseId": "decision-alerts",
      "kind": "task",
