    {
      "id": "ee2e49d6",
      "title": "Bug: card list --open shows a track card as open after the PM confirmed the track",
      "status": "backlog",
      "componentId": "agent-tooling",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-08T20:33:57.663Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-08T20:34:11.431Z",
      "order": 17,
      "kind": "bug",
      "role": "backend-engineer",
      "description": "Proposed track: Bugfix. Plan: after decision-alerts (sprint 2026-w43). Not ready to build: needs the PM's track confirmation, then `specs/bugs/ee2e49d6/bugfix.md` and a failing regression test from the qa-engineer.\n\nObserved (EM, 2026-10-09): `project-companion card list --open` shows `c-31ea34 open decision-alerts Which track should Decision alerts take?`, but `gate status` shows `track decision-alerts full`. The PM confirmed the track; the card still shows as open and stays in the PM's list.\nWhere: `cli/index.ts:1470` keeps a card when `c.answer === undefined`. A track is confirmed by a track gate event, not a `card.answered` event, so a track card never gets an answer (`foldCards` in `lib/project/decisions.ts`).\nExpected: a track card is closed when its subject's track is confirmed. Check the cockpit's \"needs you\" list too, if it uses the same rule. The requirement ID is for the qa-engineer to find; if none exists, write UNKNOWN and tell the EM."
    },
    {
      "id": "d5ebde85",
      "title": "Bug: the artifact text lookup can be slow without limit (SR-8)",
      "status": "backlog",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-08T20:33:57.740Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-08T20:34:22.920Z",
      "order": 18,
      "kind": "bug",
      "role": "backend-engineer",
      "description": "Proposed track: Bugfix. Plan: after decision-alerts (sprint 2026-w43). It must come after the feature: design section 3 (`specs/decision-alerts/design.md:453`) says the SR-8 fix changes how `hashArtifact` reads files, and must update a decision-alerts test. Not ready to build: needs the PM's track confirmation, then `specs/bugs/d5ebde85/bugfix.md` and a failing regression test from the qa-engineer.\n\nSource: security review SR-8 (`specs/decision-alerts/reviews/security.md:108`), design section 6 step 5 (`specs/decision-alerts/design.md:513`), both approved at the design gate.\nObserved: the text lookup re-hashes every approved artifact. An artifact path from a merged log can name a very large file or a device such as `/dev/zero` (`join(root, ref)` accepts `..`). Then `gate request` (`lib/project/gate.ts:257`), and after da-t7 also `card open`, are slow without limit or never end.\nFix (from SR-8): accept only artifact paths and a PRD source that are regular files inside the project root.\nNote: `lib/project/gate.ts` belongs to no component."
    },
    {
      "id": "5bf8eb1b",
      "title": "Run CI on every pull request: npm ci, typecheck, npm test, build:tools",
      "description": "Track: Quick (epic ci), confirmed by the PM on 2026-10-09. Spec: specs/ci/quick.md (CI-01.1 to CI-01.9). Not ready to build until the PM signs off the spec (constitution rule 4).\n\nOrder: sprint 2026-w42, order 0, before da-t1 (cc05f85e). It must merge before the first build pull request, so every build PR runs CI. The merge gate runs `gh pr checks` and refuses a PR with no checks.\n\nScope (from the PM, 2026-10-09): a GitHub Actions workflow that runs on every pull request: npm ci, typecheck, npm test, npm run build:tools. The spec adds CI-01.9 (the job token can only read the repository).\n\nKnown facts:\n- There is no .github/workflows/ folder and no typecheck script in package.json.\n- Typecheck FAILS on a clean checkout: `npx tsc --noEmit` exit 2, TS2307 `./icon-data.json` (lib/arch/icons/resolve.tsx:60). The file is generated by `npm run build:icons` and is in .gitignore. After build:icons, exit 0. (product-manager, clean export of 0e7600d.) The EM's earlier \"exit 0\" was from a working copy that already had the file.\n- Clean export: `npm run build:tools` exit 0; `PROJECT_COMPANION_NOTIFY=off npm test` exit 0 (21 s). On a GitHub runner: not checked.\n- devops-sre may write .github/workflows/**, package.json and docs/runbooks/** (.claude/harness.json). No component owns .github/workflows/ or package.json.\n\nEstimate: about 35 changed lines plus a short runbook, 2 points (product-manager estimate; reasoning in its hand-off).\nDocs (rule 12): the same PR adds a short runbook, docs/runbooks/ci.md: what the ci check runs, how to run it locally, how to roll back.\n\nVerify: the Verify lines for CI-01.1 to CI-01.9 in specs/ci/quick.md.",
